course: dictionary
lesson: 882
title: What is a biography?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A biography is a true book or story about a real person's life, written by someone else. In the example, «The story of young George Washington, later the first President of the USA» is about a real man. The word «biography» tells you the book is about someone who really lived.
explain: Because a biography is non-fiction, it uses facts, dates and the order in which things happened. A writer often starts with when and where the person was born, then moves through school, work and later life.
explain: Be careful, though. The cherry tree story «first appeared in Mason Locke Weems's biography (1806 edition) and is almost certainly invented.» So a biography about a real person can still include a made-up story. A good reader checks facts against other sources.
explain: The word can also mean a short description of someone's life, such as on a book cover or website. The adjective is biographical, as in a biographical account of a famous person.
fact: A biography is a true book or story about a real person's life, written by someone else.
fact: A biography is non-fiction, so it uses facts, dates and the order of events.
fact: A short biography is a brief description of a person's life, such as on a book cover or website.
fact: «Biographies» is the plural of biography, and «biographical» is the adjective.
fact: Not every story in a biography is always true: «the cherry tree story is almost certainly invented», so check facts with other sources.
exercise: What is a biography? | A made-up story about a magic land | *A true book or story about a real person's life, written by someone else | A poem about the seasons | A list of rules for a game
exercise: Find and copy the word that means more than one biography. | cherry | *biographies | Washington | biographical
exercise: Why is a biography non-fiction? | *Because it uses real facts, dates and the order of events | Because it always rhymes | Because it has a dragon in it | Because it is written in a secret code
test: Which of these is a true book about a real person's life? | *A biography of Mary Seacole | A comic about aliens | A story about a talking fox | A fairy tale about a princess
test: Which word is the adjective? | a biography | biographies | biography | *biographical
exam: The story of George Washington and the cherry tree is almost certainly invented, so what should a careful reader do? | Decide it must be a poem | Throw the book away without reading it | *Check the facts against other sources | Believe every word because it is printed in a book
